1
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,950
Today's the day I'll finally ask 
Kamegawa out for drinks.

2
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:18,800
"As..."

3
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,510
"As a thank-you for lending me your 
umbrella, want to go out for drinks?"

4
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:23,850
"As a thank-you for 
lending me your umbrella..."

5
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:26,350
Would it be better if I said it's my treat?

6
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:27,730
Hmm...

7
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:31,660
So then I entered the raffle, and I won!

8
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:33,380
Wow! That's amazing!

9
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:37,470
<i>Kamegawa and... Who is that?</i>

10
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:40,390
<i>Maybe a new hire like him?</i>

11
00:00:41,130 --> 00:00:44,640
<i>I bet it's easier to get along with 
people in the same age group.</i>

12
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:46,060
<i>Huh?!</i>

13
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:48,740
<i>Wait, why am I feeling down about this?</i>

14
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:53,740
<i>As a mature adult, I should be happy 
to see coworkers getting along smoothly.</i>

15
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:55,530
<i>You got this, Kamegawa!</i>

16
00:00:55,530 --> 00:00:58,030
A fireworks festival, huh? I'm excited!

17
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:00,570
You should be thankful 
for my insanely good luck!

18
00:01:00,570 --> 00:01:03,000
Thank you, O great Hotta-sama!

19
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,600
It's been a while since 
I went to see fireworks.

20
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:13,850
<i>Guess I'll invite him out 
for drinks some other time.</i>

21
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:17,050
What's this? Are you guys going 
to the fireworks festival, too?

22
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:19,010
Wha—

23
00:01:19,010 --> 00:01:21,260
Can we go with you?

24
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:23,970
What?!

25
00:01:25,430 --> 00:01:29,110
MY AWKWARD SENPAI

26
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:59,030
EPISODE 6:
 A YUKATA IS THE NORM FOR FIREWORKS FESTIVALS

27
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:57,920
"A Yukata Is the Norm For Fireworks Festivals."

28
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:02,530
<i>Who butts into the conversation 
of a couple of coworkers</i>

29
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:04,800
<i>hyped up about goin' to see the fireworks?!</i>

30
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,820
<i>Are they insane?!</i>

31
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:07,540
<i>Don't get in their way!</i>

32
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:10,290
Oh, yes. If you two don't mind.

33
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:11,870
We may be in different departments,

34
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:14,420
but this would be a nice opportunity 
to get to know each other.

35
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:17,260
<i>Whaddya mean, "get to know each other"?!</i>

36
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:18,880
<i>Read the room! Idiot!</i>

37
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:21,880
Thank you. I feel the same.

38
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,690
Where should we meet up?

39
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:25,140
Can we pick the spot?

40
00:03:25,490 --> 00:03:27,130
Um...

41
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:30,140
I'll leave that to you, then.

42
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:31,020
<i>Oh, no!</i>

43
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:33,100
<i>They're going deeper into the plan!</i>

44
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:35,090
Give me your contact info, then.

45
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:35,830
Hey.

46
00:03:37,850 --> 00:03:39,580
This fireworks festival...

47
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:43,110
Mind if I join you?

48
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:46,920
Oh, um... Not at all...

49
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:51,010
Oh! But it'll be harder to 
get around in a larger group!

50
00:03:51,010 --> 00:03:52,410
Y-You're right!

51
00:03:52,410 --> 00:03:54,540
We'll have to skip it this time.

52
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:55,600
Maybe next time!

53
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,020
Later.

54
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:59,580
What? Um, okay...

55
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:05,890
HEH, HEH, HEH

56
00:04:01,090 --> 00:04:02,410
<i>Behold.</i>

57
00:04:02,410 --> 00:04:06,090
<i>A skill that's only achievable 
for people who are outcasts...</i>

58
00:04:05,930 --> 00:04:07,140
SOBS

59
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,700
Um, Senpai...

60
00:04:09,210 --> 00:04:12,290
I was lying about wanting to go.

61
00:04:12,290 --> 00:04:13,210
Don't worry about it.

62
00:04:13,210 --> 00:04:13,770
Huh?

63
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:16,240
It's your long-awaited fireworks festival.

64
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:18,270
You two should enjoy it together.

65
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:23,390
<i>Could it be that...</i>

66
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:25,820
<i>they actually wanted to go with those two?!</i>

67
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:28,450
<i>If this turns out to be a 
huge misunderstanding, I...</i>

68
00:04:28,910 --> 00:04:32,100
<i>Oh, no... I should have 
minded my own business.</i>

69
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:33,360
Um, Senpai!

70
00:04:33,870 --> 00:04:35,330
Wh-What is it?

71
00:04:35,950 --> 00:04:37,940
Would you like to join us, Senpai?

72
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:39,210
At the fireworks festival!

73
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:43,170
Nice to meet you. I'm Mio Hotta.

74
00:04:43,170 --> 00:04:46,960
I'm in the Public Relations Department 
and started at the same time as Kamegawa.

75
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,600
It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance!

76
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:50,600
I'm Azusa Kannawa.

77
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,440
It feels as if it's not our first time meeting.

78
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:54,350
PUBLIC RELATIONS DEPARTMENT - MIO HOTTA

79
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:56,410
I've heard so much about you from Kamegawa.

80
00:04:56,410 --> 00:04:57,180
Hey!

81
00:04:57,180 --> 00:05:00,190
Senpai's busy, so let's 
move on to the festival...

82
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:05,200
I was able to win the seated spots 
for this fireworks festival!

83
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:05,200
FIREWORKS FESTIVAL - ENTRY RESULTS

84
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,200
ENTRY RESULTS 
WINNER - CONGRATULATIONS

85
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,510
<i>Wow.</i>

86
00:05:08,510 --> 00:05:12,430
<i>I didn't know fireworks festivals these 
days needed reservations in advance.</i>

87
00:05:12,830 --> 00:05:17,210
<i>Well, not like I've been to 
one since I was a li'l kid.</i>

88
00:05:17,210 --> 00:05:21,210
Hotta suggested that we new 
hires should all go together.

89
00:05:21,210 --> 00:05:23,320
Huh? All the new hires?

90
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:24,270
Yes, ma'am!

91
00:05:24,270 --> 00:05:26,470
All six of us, including Kamegawa and me.

92
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:28,990
<i>So it wasn't gonna be just the two of 'em...</i>

93
00:05:28,990 --> 00:05:29,700
<i>No, wait.</i>

94
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:34,080
<i>It's gonna awkward insertin' 
myself in a group of six juniors.</i>

95
00:05:34,570 --> 00:05:38,370
Wouldn't it be better for the newbies 
to have fun with each other

96
00:05:38,370 --> 00:05:39,480
without an outsider like me?

97
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:41,770
Please don't worry about it!

98
00:05:41,770 --> 00:05:46,200
I've been wanting to talk with you 
for a while now, Kannawa-senpai!

99
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:48,080
Wh-Why?

100
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,330
Aren't we talking right now?

101
00:05:51,850 --> 00:05:56,000
Oh, I'm sure Senpai must be 
tired and all, so... Right?

102
00:05:56,790 --> 00:05:59,750
I'm looking forward to it, Kannawa-senpai!

103
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:03,710
Y-Yeah. Me, too.

104
00:06:12,210 --> 00:06:14,040
It's a festival, so...

105
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:16,980
Of course people would wear yukata.

106
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:21,700
I've no idea what would be good.

107
00:06:22,270 --> 00:06:28,240
Come to think of it, I do have that one 
Mom bought me ages ago that I never wore.

108
00:06:32,410 --> 00:06:34,410
MOM - CALLING

109
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:36,260
<i>Hello!</i>

110
00:06:36,260 --> 00:06:37,060
Hi, Mom—

111
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:40,590
<i>Getting a call from you is so rare, Azusa-chan!</i>

112
00:06:39,710 --> 00:06:43,130
UGH...

113
00:06:40,590 --> 00:06:41,880
<i>Are you doin' good?</i>

114
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:43,660
<i>Are ya off work for the day?</i>

115
00:06:43,660 --> 00:06:45,020
<i>What's the matter?</i>

116
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:47,860
Oh, yeah, um... Hey, Mom?

117
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:49,630
That yukata you got me a while back—

118
00:06:49,630 --> 00:06:51,120
<i>Yukata!</i>

119
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,820
<i>That yukata, yeah!</i>

120
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:55,220
<i>It was love at first sight, so I bought it.</i>

121
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:58,200
<i>But you ended up movin' to Tokyo 
without even wearin' it once.</i>

122
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:00,180
<i>Wait! Do you need it?</i>

123
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:04,480
Yeah. So could ya send me 
a photo of the yukata?

124
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,730
<i>Could it be a date?!</i>

125
00:07:06,730 --> 00:07:07,790
No!

126
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:11,920
I-I'm just going to a fireworks festival 
with some people from work!

127
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:13,120
<i>Really?</i>

128
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:15,400
<i>I guess some work places do that.</i>

129
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:18,030
<i>Oh, I just sent ya the photo!</i>

130
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:24,740
Never mind. Sorry.

131
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:26,970
It's a li'l too cutesy for me.

132
00:07:26,970 --> 00:07:28,110
<i>Really?</i>

133
00:07:28,110 --> 00:07:31,570
<i>I even have the hair piece, bag, 
and geta that go with it!</i>

134
00:07:31,570 --> 00:07:33,510
Oh. Then can you send me those?

135
00:07:33,510 --> 00:07:34,720
<i>Okay!</i>

136
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:38,800
<i>I'll send ya some cash, 
so go buy yourself a new yukata!</i>

137
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:41,730
I'm a working adult.

138
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:43,960
It's okay. I can buy it with my own money.

139
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:45,560
<i>Yer right!</i>

140
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:49,540
<i>Since all you do is play games and never leave 
the house, you've got the money to spend!</i>

141
00:07:58,790 --> 00:08:00,620
Wh-Whoa...

142
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:04,740
<i>I dunno what to pick, or how...</i>

143
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:07,920
<i>I don't even know what I'm doing 
when I need to buy normal clothes.</i>

144
00:08:08,370 --> 00:08:10,590
Are you shopping for a yukata today?

145
00:08:11,570 --> 00:08:14,600
This area is our new release section.

146
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:16,510
What kind of style are you looking for?

147
00:08:16,510 --> 00:08:17,960
I'm all right.

148
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:24,530
Please feel free to let me 
know if you need any help.

149
00:08:24,530 --> 00:08:25,240
Sure.

150
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:28,300
<i>I'm so sorry, Ms. Employee Person...</i>

151
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:30,480
<i>She's just doin' her job...</i>

152
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:39,420
<i>Kame (turtle)...</i>

153
00:08:40,010 --> 00:08:42,230
<i>I wonder what Kamegawa will...</i>

154
00:08:43,250 --> 00:08:46,610
Wait! Why was I reminded of Kamegawa?!

155
00:08:46,610 --> 00:08:47,730
It's okay!

156
00:08:47,730 --> 00:08:50,510
I may not know what to wear, 
but I need <i>something</i>!

157
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:52,010
In situations like this...

158
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,590
Excuse me! I'll take this one!

159
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:01,010
EVEN BEGINNERS CAN DO IT!!
HOW TO PUT ON A YUKATA

160
00:09:03,970 --> 00:09:04,880
Hm?

161
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:07,880
The right side goes over the 
top and... the left is under?

162
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,390
Wait, which is which for me right now?

163
00:09:10,390 --> 00:09:12,530
H-Here? Hm? Huh?

164
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:18,530
I thought I could do this by myself, 
but I could use two more hands!

165
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:21,030
AN HOUR LATER

166
00:09:26,510 --> 00:09:27,540
I can't do this...

167
00:09:30,950 --> 00:09:32,190
Skitter, skitter...

168
00:09:33,770 --> 00:09:37,180
Oh? Good morning, Kannawa-senpai!

169
00:09:38,430 --> 00:09:40,680
M-May I speak with you for a bit?

170
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:41,620
Of course!

171
00:09:43,090 --> 00:09:46,170
You see... About the fireworks festival...

172
00:09:46,170 --> 00:09:46,750
Huh?!

173
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:48,810
Could it be that you have other plans?

174
00:09:48,810 --> 00:09:50,440
No, I don't!

175
00:09:51,470 --> 00:09:53,860
I bought a yukata, and...

176
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:57,200
What? Are you going to wear a yukata, Senpai?

177
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:58,960
Aren't you?

178
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:01,760
I was thinking of just 
going in my regular clothes.

179
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:04,330
<i>I-I could have just chosen to 
wear my normal clothes?</i>

180
00:10:04,750 --> 00:10:09,580
AAAAAAAHHH

181
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:06,730
<i>Since I went out to get a yukata,</i>

182
00:10:06,730 --> 00:10:09,580
<i>now I look like someone 
who's super excited to go!</i>

183
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:13,090
If you're going to wear a yukata, 
I'll wear mine, too!

184
00:10:13,090 --> 00:10:13,890
Huh?

185
00:10:13,890 --> 00:10:18,590
Well, I was also thinking of wearing 
one since it's a good opportunity,

186
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:21,660
but I figured everyone else would 
be wearing regular clothes,

187
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:24,080
so I thought if I was the only 
one wearing a yukata...

188
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:28,980
Which is why I'm so happy to hear 
that you're going to wear yours!

189
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:30,900
R-Really?

190
00:10:31,670 --> 00:10:33,230
Oh, sorry.

191
00:10:33,750 --> 00:10:35,660
You were saying... about buying a yukata?

192
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:40,530
Oh, um... How are you going to put it on?

193
00:10:40,530 --> 00:10:41,680
Hmm...

194
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:46,240
Some salons can get you ready along 
with your yukata if you bring it, I think?

195
00:10:46,570 --> 00:10:50,250
But nowadays, there are tutorial videos online.

196
00:10:50,250 --> 00:10:52,920
Just watch those and you'll be set!

197
00:10:53,250 --> 00:10:56,050
Yeah, I suppose.

198
00:10:56,050 --> 00:10:58,310
<i>All right. Time to make a salon reservation.</i>

199
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:01,240
Hey!

200
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,970
I was just chatting with Kannawa-senpai.

201
00:11:03,970 --> 00:11:05,460
With Senpai?

202
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:08,480
What?

203
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:11,730
Look forward to Kannawa-senpai in a yukata!

204
00:11:11,730 --> 00:11:12,490
Huh?

205
00:11:14,430 --> 00:11:18,150
Senpai in a yukata! Senpai in a yukata!

206
00:11:15,590 --> 00:11:17,030
H-Hey!

207
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:20,780
A yukata...

208
00:11:22,030 --> 00:11:27,040
TODA-KOEN STATION

209
00:11:27,850 --> 00:11:30,540
You guys arrived early today!

210
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:32,010
Of course we did!

211
00:11:32,010 --> 00:11:34,510
The notorious Kannawa-senpai 
is coming, right?

212
00:11:34,510 --> 00:11:37,040
There's no way we can be late if she'll be here.

213
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:37,870
Yeah!

214
00:11:37,870 --> 00:11:40,260
So, how is she?

215
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:41,460
What do you mean?

216
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:45,510
People say she's good at her job, 
but she's also really scary.

217
00:11:45,510 --> 00:11:50,520
Well, it's true that she takes her job 
seriously and can be strict...

218
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:52,860
It's amazing that you can 
be friendly and hang out

219
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:54,970
with someone like that privately.

220
00:11:54,970 --> 00:11:58,530
Kamegawa-kun is friendly and kind, after all.

221
00:11:58,530 --> 00:12:01,360
It's not because I'm kind,
but because Senpai's—

222
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:03,450
Oh! Kannawa-senpai!

223
00:12:03,450 --> 00:12:06,570
Hey! Kannawa-senpai!

224
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,670
Sorry to keep you all waiting.

225
00:12:19,310 --> 00:12:22,600
Senpai! That yukata is super cute!

226
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,040
Yours, too.

227
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:26,240
Did you dress yourself?

228
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:29,110
Yes! I did my best by following a tutorial!

229
00:12:32,690 --> 00:12:35,650
I'm Kannawa, Kamegawa's mentor.

230
00:12:35,650 --> 00:12:39,180
I'm joining you all today 
thanks to Hotta's kind invitation.

231
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:41,740
But please don't mind me.
 Just enjoy yourselves.

232
00:12:42,210 --> 00:12:44,740
<i>Good! I was able to say it 
just like I practiced!</i>

233
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:47,000
It's nice to meet you!

234
00:12:49,350 --> 00:12:51,460
Then... let me introduce 
you to my colleagues.

235
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:52,260
I'm Takeda.

236
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:53,260
I'm Tsukano.

237
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:54,170
I'm Takigami.

238
00:12:54,170 --> 00:12:55,180
I'm Otake.

239
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:56,690
There you have it.

240
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:58,280
Hey, now.

241
00:12:57,050 --> 00:12:58,130
Come on!

242
00:12:58,130 --> 00:12:59,940
You can do better, Kamegawa.

243
00:12:58,280 --> 00:12:59,930
Get it together!

244
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:01,510
It's nice to meet you all!

245
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,960
There's still time before the fireworks.

246
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:13,200
We should get something to snack on!

247
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,450
Agreed.

248
00:13:14,450 --> 00:13:17,270
We can get something 
at the food stalls up ahead.

249
00:13:21,270 --> 00:13:25,280
YAKISOBA - CHICKEN GYOZA
 CHEWY MEAT SKEWER STICKS

250
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:28,280
CHEWY MEAT SKEWER STICKS

251
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:30,280
TAKOYAKI - YAKISOBA

252
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:34,290
YAKISOBA

253
00:13:30,660 --> 00:13:34,290
Since we have so many people, 
let's split into two groups and shop around.

254
00:13:34,290 --> 00:13:35,490
Got it.

255
00:13:35,490 --> 00:13:39,840
Kamegawa-kun, Hotta-san, 
and Kannawa-san can be a group.

256
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:40,880
Okay!

257
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:44,640
<i>I told 'em not to worry about me, 
but I guess they can't avoid it.</i>

258
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:45,920
<i>I feel bad.</i>

259
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:49,640
NORMAL - ONION - MAYO - CHEESE - EGG

260
00:13:46,970 --> 00:13:49,640
Is there anything you want to eat, Senpai?

261
00:13:50,850 --> 00:13:51,760
Cold noodles.

262
00:13:52,030 --> 00:13:53,270
Cold noodles?!

263
00:13:53,770 --> 00:14:07,780
TAKOYAKI - YAKISOBA MADE FOR KINGS

264
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:56,290
What about takoyaki, Senpai?

265
00:13:56,290 --> 00:13:59,240
If we're eating festival foods, 
doughy stuff is the best!

266
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,330
No objections!

267
00:14:00,330 --> 00:14:02,590
Oh, but I want to try a bunch of stuff,

268
00:14:02,590 --> 00:14:05,550
so is it okay if we buy one 
of each thing and share?

269
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:07,780
If Senpai is okay with that.

270
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:09,280
Go buy some with this.

271
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:10,040
What?

272
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:11,300
No, we couldn't!

273
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:12,280
Yeah!

274
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:15,290
You guys invited me to your hangout.

275
00:14:15,290 --> 00:14:17,410
This is the least I can do.

276
00:14:17,410 --> 00:14:20,520
But this is outside of work...

277
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:24,200
Stall food isn't cheap!

278
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:25,260
FLASH

279
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:31,060
If you get too caught up in buying stuff, 
you'll be broke before you know it!

280
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:32,760
Thank you so much!

281
00:14:33,990 --> 00:14:37,150
We get the whole wallet! She's so cool!

282
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:44,280
Let's eat while they're still hot, Senpai!

283
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,280
Yeah.

284
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:46,980
Let's eat!

285
00:14:55,290 --> 00:14:57,450
A-Aren't they hot?

286
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,300
They are, but...

287
00:14:59,300 --> 00:15:02,080
If you eat them and 
simultaneously inhale air...

288
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:11,770
S-Senpai! Are you okay?!

289
00:15:11,770 --> 00:15:12,820
Water! Something to drink!

290
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:13,780
Oh, no! I don't have any!

291
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:15,180
I'll go buy something!

292
00:15:16,810 --> 00:15:19,310
Much better...

293
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:21,930
S-Sorry to make you worry.

294
00:15:21,930 --> 00:15:24,300
I'm sorry I said they were okay.

295
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:25,690
What a relief.

296
00:15:27,950 --> 00:15:31,890
I wonder why stall foods are so tasty.

297
00:15:31,890 --> 00:15:33,920
It's gotta be the vibes.

298
00:15:33,920 --> 00:15:37,140
They also have foods that 
you wouldn't normally eat.

299
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:40,930
But even so, I feel like 
I eat yakisoba regularly.

300
00:15:40,930 --> 00:15:43,050
I bet it's just instant yakisoba!

301
00:15:43,050 --> 00:15:44,740
Especially since you had 
to budget your food

302
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:46,710
during training because 
you bought some toys.

303
00:15:46,710 --> 00:15:49,340
Did you know that, Kannawa-senpai?

304
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:51,720
That Kamegawa likes plastic model kits.

305
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:53,400
Oh, I knew that.

306
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:53,400
She knows!

307
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:54,470
Senpai knows!

308
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:57,960
Besides, I'm cooking my own 
meals as much as I can now.

309
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:58,810
Really?

310
00:15:58,810 --> 00:15:59,810
Yes, really!

311
00:15:59,810 --> 00:16:05,020
<i>Huh... So Kamegawa can talk like this...</i>

312
00:15:59,810 --> 00:16:02,230
Well, sure. We can leave it at that.

313
00:16:02,230 --> 00:16:04,010
What do you mean we "can"?

314
00:16:04,010 --> 00:16:06,230
I guess anyone would pretend 
they're doing better.

315
00:16:09,180 --> 00:16:11,100
Oh! Shooting!

316
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:12,330
What do you say, Senpai?

317
00:16:12,330 --> 00:16:13,860
A match between the three of us!

318
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:16,850
You two go ahead. I'll watch.

319
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:17,970
Really?

320
00:16:17,970 --> 00:16:21,320
Is there anything you want, then, Senpai?

321
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,120
Huh?

322
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:23,480
Um...

323
00:16:24,130 --> 00:16:26,100
I'm not going to hold back!

324
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:28,100
That's my line.

325
00:16:28,100 --> 00:16:30,770
What'll it be, Kannawa-senpai?

326
00:16:30,770 --> 00:16:33,420
Th-Then...

327
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:35,300
One of the plushies...

328
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:36,510
Got it!

329
00:16:37,610 --> 00:16:39,230
Huh? I can't hit it...

330
00:16:39,230 --> 00:16:41,030
Just a little more...

331
00:16:41,030 --> 00:16:43,310
Hey! That's the one I'm after!

332
00:16:43,310 --> 00:16:46,650
<i>They're both good juniors... And so kind.</i>

333
00:16:47,490 --> 00:16:53,690
<i>I know that I'm in the wrong 
for having these thoughts... but...</i>

334
00:16:56,930 --> 00:16:59,740
<i>I can't bring myself to 
be a part of their world.</i>

335
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:07,440
<i>What am I doin'?</i>

336
00:17:07,990 --> 00:17:09,790
<i>What am I thinkin'?</i>

337
00:17:10,190 --> 00:17:12,600
<i>And what am I feelin'?</i>

338
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:20,140
<i>I'll just wander around on my own.</i>

339
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:24,420
<i>And later, when we regroup, 
I can say I got lost or something...</i>

340
00:17:30,890 --> 00:17:32,780
Now I've done it.

341
00:17:34,670 --> 00:17:37,590
And now I'm really lost.

342
00:17:38,850 --> 00:17:42,290
<i>If I can just make it to the 
fireworks festival grounds...</i>

343
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:44,180
Huh?

344
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:47,260
Oh, no! I forgot to charge my phone!

345
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:54,800
I should've bought new geta instead.

346
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:03,310
<i>I'm used to being alone, but...</i>

347
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:07,790
<i>Even on field trips,
I always ate my meals alone.</i>

348
00:18:07,790 --> 00:18:12,820
<i>And on school trips, I'd stray from 
my group to spend time by myself.</i>

349
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,820
<i>So then...</i>

350
00:18:15,210 --> 00:18:18,020
<i>Why do I feel so down?</i>

351
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:21,260
<i>Kamegawa's just my junior.</i>

352
00:18:21,260 --> 00:18:23,980
<i>There's no reason for me to get along 
with him more than I need to.</i>

353
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:25,080
<i>So why?</i>

354
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,830
Oh! There she is!

355
00:18:26,830 --> 00:18:30,370
I looked all over for you, Kannawa-senpai!

356
00:18:30,370 --> 00:18:31,540
Hotta...

357
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:34,230
You had me worried, 
disappearing all of a sudden.

358
00:18:34,630 --> 00:18:35,300
Whoa!

359
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:37,090
Your strap's broken!

360
00:18:37,470 --> 00:18:38,500
Sorry.

361
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:41,340
I got distracted by this and then 
realized I was separated from you two.

362
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:43,920
No, no! I'm sorry I didn't notice!

363
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:46,100
No, I'm really sorry.

364
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:49,970
Your phone's dead, right, Kannawa-senpai?

365
00:18:49,970 --> 00:18:52,610
I'll let Kamegawa know.

366
00:18:52,610 --> 00:18:54,330
O-Okay.

367
00:18:55,860 --> 00:18:58,830
Oh, I found her. Under the Toda Bridge.

368
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:02,410
Yeah. Call me again if you can't find it.

369
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:06,480
Kamegawa was super worried.
He's been looking all over for you.

370
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:07,130
What?

371
00:19:08,390 --> 00:19:09,760
I'm sorry.

372
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:13,500
I intruded on your get-together 
only for this to happen...

373
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:17,050
It's really okay!

374
00:19:17,050 --> 00:19:19,470
In fact, I'm honored to 
be able to talk with you!

375
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:22,880
You were saying that before, too.

376
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:25,220
But there's nothing to gain
from talking with me.

377
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:26,900
That's not true!

378
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:28,980
Kamegawa says so all the time!

379
00:19:30,010 --> 00:19:32,890
Whenever he opens his mouth, 
he says stuff like, "Senpai is nice,"

380
00:19:32,890 --> 00:19:35,480
or "Senpai taught me this in detail."

381
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:39,240
He always follows up 
with "thanks to Senpai."

382
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:43,300
He really respects you, Kannawa-senpai.

383
00:19:43,710 --> 00:19:46,740
But you know... since I'm in a 
different department from you two...

384
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:51,730
To be honest, I often heard the 
opposite about you from the rumors.

385
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:53,770
Like how you were scary and strict.

386
00:19:53,770 --> 00:19:58,720
But he's not the kind of guy 
to tell lies, so I believed him.

387
00:19:58,720 --> 00:20:02,130
And then I wanted to try
 talking to you, as well.

388
00:20:02,130 --> 00:20:03,350
That's enough.

389
00:20:04,390 --> 00:20:06,890
You can stop with the flattery.

390
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:14,200
So Kamegawa was right all along, huh?

391
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:16,030
Wh-What gave you that impression?

392
00:20:16,030 --> 00:20:17,320
Kannawa-senpai!

393
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:19,740
Kamegawa.

394
00:20:21,190 --> 00:20:22,780
I was so worried.

395
00:20:23,070 --> 00:20:25,280
Extremely worried!

396
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:28,040
Oh, um...

397
00:20:30,610 --> 00:20:32,410
No need to go into the details!

398
00:20:32,730 --> 00:20:34,290
She's found. That's what matters.

399
00:20:34,990 --> 00:20:37,770
Besides, the fireworks are starting soon!

400
00:20:37,770 --> 00:20:39,120
We need to hurry.

401
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:42,200
Oh, sorry, but could you two go on ahead?

402
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,490
My geta strap broke.

403
00:20:44,490 --> 00:20:45,430
What?!

404
00:20:46,430 --> 00:20:47,940
I forgot!

405
00:20:47,940 --> 00:20:49,430
Let me look something up.

406
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:53,430
Let's see. You can use a handkerchief and...

407
00:20:53,430 --> 00:20:55,260
a five-yen coin...

408
00:20:55,660 --> 00:20:57,690
I'm going to borrow your wallet again, Senpai.

409
00:20:57,690 --> 00:20:58,940
What? Now?

410
00:20:59,290 --> 00:21:01,290
Can I ask for a five-yen coin?

411
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:04,520
I think we can do a temporary fix, 
so I'm going to try it.

412
00:21:04,520 --> 00:21:05,700
Okay.

413
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:10,120
Twist up a handkerchief 
until it's like a rope...

414
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:12,700
5 YEN

415
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:12,280
Put it through a five-yen coin,

416
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:15,050
then slip it from the bottom of the shoe...

417
00:21:16,290 --> 00:21:19,060
Flip it over and tie them up, and then...

418
00:21:19,670 --> 00:21:20,710
It's done!

419
00:21:22,510 --> 00:21:24,600
It should be fine now.

420
00:21:30,830 --> 00:21:32,330
This will work!

421
00:21:32,330 --> 00:21:35,100
I'm so glad. Shall we get going, then?

422
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:35,740
Yeah.

423
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:36,510
Yup!

424
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:42,170
We can still catch the first shot!

425
00:21:43,850 --> 00:21:45,060
Hold on, Hotta!

426
00:21:45,060 --> 00:21:47,030
If you pull her around like that, 
the strap could...

427
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:50,030
But you fixed it up, right?

428
00:21:50,030 --> 00:21:53,790
It's only a temporary fix! 
It could come undone!

429
00:22:12,470 --> 00:22:14,180
Don't get separated.

430
00:22:16,030 --> 00:22:17,050
Yes, ma'am.

431
00:22:21,560 --> 00:22:25,570
EAST A SEATING AREA - EAST B SEATING AREA

432
00:22:25,860 --> 00:22:30,500
Do you see Otake over there? That's our spot.

433
00:22:30,500 --> 00:22:32,030
Yeah. Gotcha.

434
00:22:32,030 --> 00:22:34,510
I'm going to go buy some drinks.

435
00:22:34,510 --> 00:22:36,100
Please go on ahead.

436
00:22:40,510 --> 00:22:41,780
S-Sorry!

437
00:22:41,780 --> 00:22:43,130
No worries.

438
00:22:45,930 --> 00:22:48,550
Um, I'm sorry about earlier.

439
00:22:48,970 --> 00:22:49,990
What?

440
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:56,720
I spoke so harshly to you when I didn't 
even realize your strap was broken.

441
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:15,880
It's so impressive from up close.

442
00:23:16,440 --> 00:23:17,440
Yeah.

443
00:23:22,490 --> 00:23:25,250
<i>Would I have been able to tell him</i>

444
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:31,010
<i>if I was his colleague and not his senpai?</i>

